{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script", "label": "ADR-018 \u2014 Contrato do bloco Python-Script", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/archive/adr/ADR-018-contrato-bloco-python-script.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script_decisao", "label": "Decision: user-defined ports (IN1..INn in, OUT1..OUTn assigned), persistent per-instance state dict, scope restricted to math+numpy, timeout ~70% of flow Ts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/archive/adr/ADR-018-contrato-bloco-python-script.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The script block is the escape valve for arbitrary logic (conditioning, selection, light interlock) without inflating the block palette. Runs via exec() in a controlled namespace on an executor (never the event loop); threat model is authenticated admin, no heavy sandboxing. Timeout/exception policy mirrors the MPC (ADR-014): hold last outputs + alarm; state survives hot-swap if the block is unchanged (ADR-011)."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script_decisao", "target": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/archive/adr/ADR-018-contrato-bloco-python-script.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script_decisao", "target": "docs_archive_adr_adr_011_hot_swap_sem_versionamento_decisao", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/archive/adr/ADR-018-contrato-bloco-python-script.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_archive_adr_adr_018_contrato_bloco_python_script_decisao", "target": "doc